  title={Systematic Approach Based on Best Practices to Develop Requirements Engineering (RE) Guideline in an Organization}, 
  year={2017},
  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={126-131},
  abstract={Best practices in developing Requirements Engineering are not new. They are easily comprehended by experts familiar to Requirements Engineering. However, for IT Personnel that are new to this field, understanding the process may pose major challenges. Thus, a Requirements Engineering Best Practices Work Flow was developed as a tool to assist in the development of Requirements Engineering. The work flow consists of four phases: Exploratory, Development, Measurement and Experts panel review. Hopefully, this Requirements Engineering Best Practices Work Flow will be a practical and helpful tool to any IT Personnel in developing Requirements Engineering in the organization.},
  keywords={Software;Requirements engineering;Best practices;Stakeholders;Guidelines;Organizations;Requirements Engineering;Software Project Approval Process;Software Requirements Specification Approval Process;Software Requirements Specification Development Procedure;Software Requirements Specification Activity Diagram;Software Project Issues;Sof},
